---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Write a note — Gloria Li" noindex>
  <div class="writer-wrap wrap" id="top">
    <div class="writer-top"><div><div class="eyebrow">YOUR WRITING DESK</div><h1>A thought starts here.</h1><p>Write in Markdown, add a little LaTeX, and see your note take shape. Your draft stays in this browser until you download it or commit it on GitHub.</p></div><a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to writing</a></div>
    <div class="writer-toolbar">
      <button class="small-button primary" id="download-note">Download .md ↓</button>
      <button class="small-button" id="github-note">Save on GitHub ↗</button>
      <button class="small-button" id="import-note">Import .md</button>
      <button class="small-button" id="copy-note">Copy Markdown</button>
      <label class="sr-only" for="saved-drafts">Restore a local draft</label><select class="small-button" id="saved-drafts"><option value="">Restore a local draft…</option></select>
      <button class="small-button discard-button" id="reset-note">New note</button>
      <input type="file" id="file-input" accept=".md,.markdown,text/markdown,text/plain" hidden />
    </div>
    <p class="writer-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">Opening your notebook…</p>
    <div class="editor-grid">
      <div class="editor-pane"><label class="editor-label" for="markdown-editor">MARKDOWN <span>+ LaTeX</span></label><textarea id="markdown-editor" spellcheck="false" aria-describedby="syntax-help"></textarea></div>
      <div class="editor-pane"><div class="editor-label">LIVE PREVIEW <span>As your readers will see it</span></div><section id="note-preview" class="preview-pane" aria-label="Note preview"></section></div>
    </div>
    <p class="writer-notice">Saving a draft here is local to this browser. To publish, use <strong>Save on GitHub</strong> to commit your note; GitHub Pages rebuilds the site automatically. Nothing is published just by typing.</p>
    <div class="writer-help" id="syntax-help">
      <div><h2>A few useful marks</h2><p><code>## A heading</code> · <code>**bold**</code> · <code>*italic*</code><br /><code>[a link](https://example.com)</code><br /><code>$x^2 + y^2$</code> for inline math.<br /><code>$$</code> on separate lines for display equations.</p><p>Use fenced code blocks with a language name for highlighted code in published posts.</p></div>
      <div><h2>From draft to published</h2><p>Keep the fields between <code>---</code> at the top. Choose a topic: <strong>Math</strong>, <strong>Machine learning</strong>, <strong>Schoolwork</strong>, or <strong>Other</strong>. Set <code>draft: false</code> when it’s ready.</p><p>Your files live in <a href="https://github.com/plumessence/plumessence.github.io/tree/main/src/content/posts" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">src/content/posts ↗</a>. You can edit them directly on GitHub at any time.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <script src="../scripts/writer.ts"></script>
</Base>
